# Cloudflare Pages redirects for the sparrowmap.com static site.
#
# 🚨 WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: sparrowmap.com/status returned 200 and served the
# LANDING PAGE. Pages falls back to index.html for any path it does not have,
# so a link that looks right, answers 200, and shows the wrong page - which is
# the worst of the three, because nothing about it looks broken.
#
# /status is the page people are sent to when someone claims the site is
# blocked, and sparrowmap.com is the domain they will type. A status link that
# quietly shows the marketing page instead would lose exactly the argument it
# was built to win.
#
# 302 rather than 301: the status page lives on the hub today, and a permanent
# redirect is cached by browsers for a long time and is painful to take back if
# that ever moves.
/status  https://map.sparrowmap.com/status  302

# The same trap, for the two paths people already share by hand.
/map     https://map.sparrowmap.com/        302
/app     https://map.sparrowmap.com/app     302
